-- ============================================================================
-- 47 (2026-06-15): NATIVE GSTA CLIENT — STAGE FLOOR/DECK rendered black; the
-- BLUE LOWER-DECK FLOOR was MARGIN-culled. Root-caused per-mesh vs the engine TA,
-- fixed the cull, and made the stage path resolve from the BINARY dir. Branch
-- feat/render-replica-live. Extends finding:native_gsta_stage_zorder (45) +
-- finding:stage_deck_texture_closed (26c).
-- ============================================================================
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:gsta_floor_cull_measure SET kind='tool',
  ref='gsta_stage.cpp emit replicated in python over atlas/stages/STG0B_ta.json + live M1/M2 from _stage_gt/ram.bin; engine GT raster _stage_gt/GROUNDTRUTH_engine_ta_STG0B.png + AFTER_ta_client_STG0B.png (tools/validate_stage_ta_client.py); GSTA shots C:/Users/trist/Downloads/_gsta_floor_*.png (build/flycast.exe MAPLECAST_GSTA_CLIENT vs headless 7212 STG0B)',
  note='PER-MESH measured ground truth (STG0B, live camera M1=[320,0,0,0; 0,-240,0,0; 0,0,-.5,0; 320,240,.5,1], M2[15]=812.36). The engine TA bake STG0B_ta.json has 72 meshes; only 3 are world-authored (mesh0 green-grid deck 726 tris tcw 0x9fc00; mesh1 48 tris; mesh3 BLUE FLOOR 2 tris tcw 0xa0000 = texture t02). The deck textures: t01(tcw 0x9fc00)=green grid + a left blue beam (meanNZ [44,112,70]); t02(tcw 0xa0000)=BLUE floor (meanNZ [14,63,149]). ENGINE GT band colours: grid-mid rgb[19,46,31] green-dom; lower-deck rgb[3,18,70] BLUE-dom; floor-strip rgb[105,107,146] blue-dom. The deck per-vertex RGB in the bake is a GREY ramp 0..252 (R==G==B) -> the colour is the TEXTURE; the grey only modulates intensity (ShadInstr=1). validate_stage_ta_client.py rasterizes the bake with the BAKED screen pos and matches the engine GT pixel-for-pixel (blue floor present) -> the bake is CORRECT, the renderer-with-baked-pos is CORRECT.';

UPSERT finding:gsta_stage_floor_cull_fix SET
  statement='THE NATIVE GSTA FLOOR/DECK WAS DARK BECAUSE THE BLUE LOWER-DECK FLOOR QUAD WAS MARGIN-CULLED — not a bake bug, not a per-vertex-colour bug, not a missing texture. ROOT CAUSE (per-mesh measured): gsta_stage.cpp gstaStageEmitTA rejected a whole triangle if ANY vertex fell outside [-MARGIN(800), 640/480+MARGIN]. mesh3 (the blue floor, texture t02 tcw 0xa0000) is 2 huge triangles spanning X +-6822 while crossing the visible bottom band (baked screen Y 362..585); the engine SUBMITS that giant quad and lets the PowerVR guard-band clip it (the captured engine TA _stage_gt/engine_ta.bin carries it at full extent), but the MARGIN=800 reject killed it -> the lit blue floor vanished. Also mesh0 (the green deck) carries 8 grazing/behind-camera verts the engine TA clamps to inv=1/w=10 with screen XY ~ -1.4e7 (pos[2]==10 sentinel); the whole-tri reject dropped every strip triangle touching one. Measured coverage of the lower-deck band (y 330..410, x 150..490): engine GT 0.41, GSTA BEFORE 0.03 (93% missing, washed-white survivors [165,156,173]). The ~"12 culled props" were these world-authored deck/floor pieces, NOT the local props (the 69 local props already rendered 68/69; the 1 miss = mesh2 entirely above the frame Y[-2600..-1041], engine-culled too). FIX (gsta_stage.cpp): replaced the per-vertex MARGIN reject with (1) a GARBAGE reject = non-finite OR |screen|>1e6 (drops the 1/w=10 sentinel verts only) and (2) a per-triangle SCREEN-BBOX-OVERLAP keep (bbox overlaps [-64,704]x[-64,544]); flycast`s rasterizer clips the off-screen remainder exactly as the engine/PVR does. This is engine-faithful: the engine TA itself submits the full floor quad. VALIDATED (cardinal rule 3, engine = arbiter): post-fix GSTA lower-deck cov 0.49..0.58 (mean 0.53) across 17 frames (f120..f600), rgb BLUE-dominant [23..57, 66..87, 137..160] (B channel dominant, matching engine [3,18,70]); floor-strip cov 0.86..0.88 (engine 0.79), rgb blue-dom [93..120,133..143,184..197] (engine [97,104,149]); ALL 4 stage bands HUE-MATCH the engine GT (grid=green-dom, deck+floor=blue-dom). The GSTA blue runs brighter than the python GT raster (hardware bilinear vs nearest-neighbour) but the structural bug (black/missing floor) is closed. Body/HUD/effects UNTOUCHED.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-15';

UPSERT finding:gsta_stage_path_from_binary SET
  statement='NATIVE GSTA STAGE PATH now resolves from the EXECUTABLE`s own directory, not just the cwd. gsta_stage.cpp gstaStageEnsureLoaded resolved STGxx_ta.json only via env override + cwd-relative bases (atlas/stages, ../atlas/stages, ../../atlas/stages) -> when the user launches build/flycast.exe from $HOME the stage silently failed to load ("[GSTA-STAGE] no bake ... stage stays unrendered"). FIX: gstaExeDir() (Win GetModuleFileNameA / Linux readlink /proc/self/exe -> dir, cached) is prepended to the candidate bases as exeDir, exeDir/atlas/stages, exeDir/../atlas/stages, exeDir/../../atlas/stages (the binary lives in build/, so build/../atlas/stages hits the repo atlas). MAPLECAST_GSTA_STAGE_DIR remains the first-priority override. The load printf now reports the resolved path. VERIFIED: launched from $HOME with NO override -> "[GSTA-STAGE] loaded STG0B ... from C:\\Users\\trist\\projects\\maplecast-flycast\\build/../atlas/stages/STG0B_ta.json". Both the env-override and binary-relative paths exercised live.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-15';

RELATE finding:gsta_stage_floor_cull_fix->cites->source:gsta_floor_cull_measure;
RELATE finding:gsta_stage_floor_cull_fix->about->finding:native_gsta_stage_zorder;
RELATE finding:gsta_stage_floor_cull_fix->about->finding:stage_deck_texture_closed;
RELATE finding:gsta_stage_path_from_binary->about->finding:native_gsta_stage_zorder;
